      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Administering insulin without a doctor's guidance can be dangerous. If your partner's blood sugar is dangerously high, it could lead to a life-threatening condition called diabetic ketoacidosis. I strongly advise against giving them insulin on your own. Instead, monitor their blood sugar closely, and if it remains high, seek emergency medical help immediately. It's always better to err on the side of caution when it comes to managing diabetes. Your partner's safety is the most important thing right now.",
      "source": "target",
